---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Acceptable Use Policy"
  description="The rules for using Davis Weather Station, including the quote form and automated access."
>
  <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    This policy protects the Site, its visitors, resellers, and service providers from abuse. It applies to everyone
    who accesses the Site, submits a quote request, or interacts with its features.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Permitted use</h2>
  <p>
    You may use the Site to browse reseller and product information, use the Smart Buying Guide, send a genuine quote
    request to a reseller, read the FAQ, and share links for personal or internal business purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Prohibited conduct</h2>
  <p>You must not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Submit spam, bulk, automated, or deceptive quote requests.</li>
    <li>Impersonate another person or misrepresent your affiliation.</li>
    <li>Use bots, scrapers, crawlers, or scripts to harvest data at scale without permission.</li>
    <li>Bypass, disable, or interfere with bot-protection controls, rate limits, or other security measures.</li>
    <li>Probe, scan, or test the vulnerability of the Site without written authorisation.</li>
    <li>Introduce malware, viruses, or harmful code.</li>
    <li>Attempt SQL injection, cross-site scripting, request forgery, or other attacks.</li>
    <li>Overload the Site, run denial-of-service tests, or disrupt service for others.</li>
    <li>Harass, threaten, defame, or discriminate against any person.</li>
    <li>Post or transmit unlawful, infringing, or misleading content.</li>
    <li>Use the Site to violate privacy, intellectual-property, or other rights.</li>
    <li>Circumvent geographic, legal, or technical restrictions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Quote form rules</h2>
  <p>
    Use the quote form only for genuine inquiries about Davis Instruments products. Provide accurate contact details
    and do not submit another person’s information without permission. Do not include payment-card data, passwords,
    government identifiers, health information, or other sensitive data.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Automated access</h2>
  <p>
    Search-engine crawlers may index public pages according to our robots directives. Other automated access —
    including scraping, data harvesting, load testing, and bulk submissions — requires prior written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Enforcement</h2>
  <p>
    We may investigate suspected violations and take any action we consider appropriate, including blocking access,
    rate-limiting, removing submissions, reporting activity to service providers or authorities, and pursuing legal
    remedies. We may preserve relevant records for investigation.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Reporting abuse</h2>
  <p>
    To report abuse, see our <a href="/report-abuse/">Report Abuse</a> page or email{' '}
    <a href="mailto:contact@davisweatherstation.com">contact@davisweatherstation.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top of this page shows the latest
    revision.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about acceptable use? Contact us through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
